cd Writing Script to Update IP address:
I learned that there can be no spaces between bash variables. I also added date so I could see when and what IP address I logged in on the pi and put the address on a new line so if I needed I can directly grep for it.

Automating Script to run on boot:
I used crontabs to automate the bash script running on reboot! It was quite convenient, and I ran into no issues. The script is update.sh under rpi/boot.